  "what": "problem PD-1@v1 drafted",
  "phase": "DISCOVER",
  "minute": 55.0,
  "event_seq": 104,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute tickets roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul) to ~1200-1260/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-06), driven primarily by a defect in the billing calculation/import-validation step that produces incorrect bills even when the underlying meter read was correctly recorded as ACTUAL: disputed bills skew toward ACTUAL (1785) over ESTIMATED (1240) reads (E-01), ruling out estimate-substitution (AMI or field read gaps) as the primary driver. No tariff change occurred this year (E-03, E-04) and ticket response times remain within SLA (E-05), so neither tariff shifts nor slow handling explain the surge; degraded manual-read route completion (0.88 vs 0.95 target, 9200 accounts, E-02) is at most a secondary contributor."
 },
