  "event_seq": 270,
  "root_problem": "Dispute tickets roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to ~1200-1260/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-06), with onset coinciding with billing-import rule BV-17 (deployed 2026-08-01), which compares raw AMI register values against 12-month m3 consumption history with no unit scaling (E-13). Because firmware v4.2 meters (rollout June 2026) report reads in 0.1 m3 sub-units rather than whole m3 (E-14), legitimate high-usage v4.2 reads are misclassified as anomalous: AMI read events for the 1240 disputed ESTIMATED-read bills show 1184 rejected at import as REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION and 56 with no accepted read, driving estimate-substitution disputes for that bucket (E-12)."
 },
